-- title:
--   Igusa chart rings inside a cusp-chart fibre model
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$, let $\ell$ be a prime not dividing $N$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that $\ell$ is a non-unit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`), whose residue field $\kappa=$ `ResidueField ↥A` has characteristic $\ell$ and is algebraically closed; write $\mathrm{red}=$ `residue ↥A` for the reduction $A\to\kappa$. The assertion is the existence of a fibre model `fm` of type `CharPModel.FibreModel N A ℓ κ red`, i.e. two subrings $B_{\mathrm{fin}},B_\infty$ of `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (modularFunctionFieldFull N)` (the field generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ by the coefficientwise image of the full modular function field $F=\mathbb{Q}(\mathrm{divisorExpansions}\,N)$) containing the constants from $A$, with $\bar j,\bar j_N\in B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $\bar j^{-1}\in B_\infty$, all of whose elements are integral over the respective affine base rings, together with ring homomorphisms $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}},\pi_\infty$ to `modularFunctionFieldC κ N` matching $\mathrm{red}$ on constants and sending $\bar j,\bar j_N,\bar j^{-1}$ to $j(q),j(q^N),j(q)^{-1}$ mod $\ell$, and of a proof that `fm` is a `CuspChart`, i.e. $\bar j_N\cdot(\bar j^{-1})^N\in B_\infty$ with $\pi_\infty$ of it equal to $j(q^N)\,j(q)^{-N}$ over $\kappa$; such that, moreover, (i) the coefficientwise image `coeffEmb` of every element of the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra `chartAlgFin N ℓ` $=$ `chartAlg N ℓ {jFull N}` of $F$ lies in $B_{\mathrm{fin}}$, (ii) likewise `chartAlgInf N ℓ` $=$ `chartAlg N ℓ {(jFull N)⁻¹}` maps into $B_\infty$, (iii) every $b\in B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ is, as a Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, equal to some $f$ in the localised modular ring `CharPReduction.modularLocalized N A.toSubring red` (the localisation, at the complement of the kernel of coefficientwise reduction, of the subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the constants from $A$ together with $j(q)$ and $j(q^N)$) with $\pi_{\mathrm{fin}}(b)=$ `modularRedLocHom` $(f)$, and (iv) the same for every $b\in B_\infty$ with $\pi_\infty$.
--
--   This is the reduction-of-$q$-expansions description of the special fibre of $X_0(N)$ at a prime $\ell\nmid N$ of good reduction, in the form asserting that the two Igusa chart rings land in a single fibre model carrying a cusp chart, and that both of the model's reduction maps are restrictions of one coefficientwise reduction homomorphism on the localised modular ring. It is used to glue the two special-fibre chart isomorphisms over the middle chart, and is cited in the construction of the residue-field base change of the chart algebras and of the special-fibre data with cusp chart for the Igusa scheme.
